// Basic: Rig's first library, written in Rig over a thin layer of C
// (libc.rig). It gathers what most programs need first: for now, numbers
// to text and back, and printing to standard output.
//
// A program loads all of it through this file, by its path from the
// program's own directory, until Rig has #import: from tests/run that is
//
//     #load "../../modules/Basic/module.rig";
//
// Loading is #load (spec 2.13), so every name Basic declares joins the
// program's one top level: a program that loads Basic can't declare a
// procedure, struct or constant of a name Basic uses. README.md lists them.
//
// Each part loads the parts it uses itself, and a file is read once however
// often it is named, so the order here is only the reading order.
#load "libc.rig";
#load "numbers.rig";
#load "print.rig";
